&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;US President Donald Trump has claimed that Iran asked the United States to stop killing its leaders, saying Washington would comply, even as American forces carried out strikes on Iran's Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz on Monday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Speaking at an event near the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool on November 2, a day before the US midterm elections, Trump declared that the US had won its war with Iran and claimed that Washington had strong control over the strategically important Strait of Hormuz.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;He added that the US had eliminated Iran's top leadership and that Tehran had asked Washington to stop targeting its leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
